  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Four people broke into the Pantheon to repair its clock. Paris, the mid-2000s. Nobody hired them, and nobody asked.",
        "visual_query": "paris pantheon neoclassical dome exterior",
        "visual_fallback": "paris monument"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Its clock had sat dead since the 1960s. So they built a workshop up under the dome and worked there for about a year.",
        "visual_query": "historic dome interior stone stairs",
        "visual_fallback": "dome interior"
      },
      {
        "narration": "One of them, Jean-Baptiste Viot, was a professional clockmaker. He took the mechanism apart piece by piece. Who breaks in to do unpaid maintenance?",
        "visual_query": "antique clock mechanism brass gears",
        "visual_fallback": "clock gears"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They call themselves Untergunther, part of a Paris underground network that quietly restores neglected heritage. When the clock ran again, they went and told the management themselves.",
        "visual_query": "paris underground tunnel stone passage",
        "visual_fallback": "stone tunnel"
      },
      {
        "narration": "France took them to court for it. The judge ruled in their favour in about twenty minutes, and years later Viot won the official contract to restore the same clock.",
        "visual_query": "paris street courthouse facade",
        "visual_fallback": "paris street"
      }
    ],
